Description: Differential expression analysis of RNA-seq count data with
    few or no replicates per condition. Extends the local pooled error (LPE)
    test (Jain et al. 2003 <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btg264>; Gim et al.
    2016 <doi:10.1371/journal.pone.0159182>) from two-group comparisons to
    one-way and additive multi-factor designs without interaction terms,
    specified via a formula such as ~ group or ~ genotype + treatment. An
    intensity-dependent variance trend is estimated from replicate pairs
    pooled across genes, with standardized between-cell differences and
    fixed-threshold trimming when design cells lack replication, and is used
    in term-specific Type II ANOVA-like tests. One-way designs can use a
    Welch-type statistic with pooled or group-specific variance trends.
    Gene-wise standard ANOVA is selected automatically when every design
    cell is well replicated. A pseudo-bulk workflow aggregates annotated
    single-cell data by sample and cell type, with optional counts per
    1,000 cells scaling. Count filtering and library-size, TMM or DESeq2
    normalization are provided, together with a Shiny interface.
